@startuml commit_addition_limit
' Pre-change source evidence: .github/workflows/ci.yml:3-24, scripts/check-commit-additions.sh:40-202, and scripts/tests/check-commit-additions-test.sh:109-116 at 2df1ffd0b15044221ea1facd43b0797f5cdbb098.
' Reviewed implementation evidence: scripts/check-commit-additions.sh:53-132 and scripts/tests/check-commit-additions-test.sh:109-133 at e7b68fd5a1b9c4699d30635d06b9467f3b8bdf2f.
' Observed behavior: CI enforced the 2000-line limit independently for each commit.
' Product constraint: the final pull-request additions must not exceed 2000 code lines in total.
' Architecture change: the gate measures one final diff from the merge base to the pull-request head.
' Design reason: prevent commit splitting from bypassing the pull-request review-size limit.
title Pull-request addition limit

actor Contributor
participant "GitHub Actions" as Actions
database "Git history" as Git
participant "Pull-request addition gate" as Gate
participant "Existing build gates" as Build

Contributor -> Actions: Push pull-request changes
Actions -> Git: Checkout full history
Actions -> Gate: Provide base SHA and head SHA
Gate -> Git: Validate revisions
Gate -> Git: Resolve merge base
Gate -> Git: Read rename-aware final diff numstat
Gate -> Gate: Classify old and new paths

opt Documentation moved into code
  Gate -> Git: Read full destination blob at head
end

Gate -> Gate: Sum final added code lines
alt Total exceeds 2000
  Gate --> Actions: Fail with total and file details
else Total is at most 2000
  Gate --> Actions: Report pull-request pass
end

Actions -> Gate: Run gate regression tests
Actions -> Build: Set up JDK, format check, verify
Build --> Contributor: CI result
@enduml
